# Tern: Content (the instrument)

- Questions, answers, nudges, notes, `did` lines, tendencies and tensions live only in `game/content.js` (park, axes, worlds, tendency library) and `game/content-<world>.js`. All 75 questions are ratified by Ken: change wording or nudges only with his say-so.
- Step keys follow the trunk answer: `trunk`, then `fu`, or `fuA`/`fuB`/`fuC`. Answer ids: `B09-A`, `B09-FUA-B`. A replaced follow-up keeps its key and gets new ids with a "2" (`Q11-FUA2-A`).
- No escape answers; a thoughtful person must hesitate; follow-ups put pressure on both sides where possible.
- Every new answer gets nudges, a `note` and a `did` line; every new tendency gets `detail`, `protect`/`trade` and a `share` line (or a deliberate decision to leave it out).
- A separate skeptic judge reviews every content pass before Ken ratifies it.
- `docs/QUESTIONS.md` is generated: after any content change run `npm run export:questions`. Never edit it by hand.
